{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-c4e4cc30-b70f-49fb-a55b-eac27354d0c4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b82c1a17ecaf7cb8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9016-4vremlud/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9016-E001.md","content":"# Idle and stale resource reports in the web console\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers per-project idle and stale resource reporting in the RHOAI\nweb console, giving cluster administrators visibility into reclaimable\ncapacity. The console gains a report surface showing, per project, workbenches\nthat have been idle (with their last activity, owner, and reserved resources)\nand pipeline runs that are stale (completed runs older than a configurable age\nthat still retain artifacts). Both reports can be exported as CSV.\n\nThe report data is sourced from existing platform telemetry: the notebook\ncontroller's per-workbench activity tracking and Kubeflow Pipelines run\ncompletion metadata. No changes are made to the notebook controller or to\nKubeflow Pipelines — both keep working as-is and serve as read-only data\nsources.\n\n## Scope\n\n- A per-project idle-workbench report in the web console listing each\n  workbench's last activity timestamp, owner, and reserved resources, sourced\n  from the notebook controller's activity tracking.\n- A per-project stale pipeline-run report listing completed runs older than a\n  configurable age that retain artifacts, sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run\n  metadata.\n- A configurable age threshold for the stale pipeline-run report.\n- CSV export of either report.\n- Read-only reporting only: no automated or UI-initiated reclamation,\n  deletion, or culling actions, and no cost/chargeback calculations (strategy\n  out of scope).\n- Screenshots or caption updates elsewhere in the console that fall out of\n  this change are updated as part of the same change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a project containing workbenches with differing activity, when an\n  administrator opens the idle-workbench report, then each workbench is listed\n  with its last activity timestamp, owner, and reserved resources, and the\n  values match the notebook controller's activity tracking for that\n  workbench.\n- Given a project containing completed pipeline runs of differing ages, when\n  an administrator opens the stale pipeline-run report with a given age\n  threshold, then only completed runs older than the threshold that retain\n  artifacts are listed, and the entries match Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n- Given the stale pipeline-run report, when an administrator changes the\n  configurable age threshold, then the report contents update accordingly.\n- Given either report, when an administrator exports it as CSV, then the\n  resulting file contains the report rows and columns as displayed.\n- Given the reports, when reviewed, then no reclamation, deletion, or cost\n  calculation actions are offered — the feature is informational only.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P1): per-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner,\n  reserved resources) sourced from the notebook controller's activity\n  tracking.\n- HLR-2 (P1): stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a\n  configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines\n  run metadata.\n- HLR-3 (P2, bundled): CSV export of either report — shares the same report\n  surfaces and data-fetch code as HLR-1/HLR-2, so it is delivered within this\n  epic rather than as a separately schedulable deliverable.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":26906,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8864edd99ad3d1ec","agent_id":"adbd529e98eccbfe5","session_id":"05ddb1e2-6b5c-4b16-a274-ad31367aa2ce","uuid":"912794ca-751a-4b47-baad-2e51ff40d864","timestamp":"2026-1