n the\n  report descriptions (columns, data sources, configurable threshold, CSV\n  export) match the implemented behavior in the web console.\n- Given an administrator following the documented reclamation steps, when the\n  steps are executed against a test project, then they are accurate and\n  complete for both idle workbenches and stale pipeline runs.\n- The documentation has been technically reviewed against the implemented\n  reports by the team that built them, and review feedback is addressed.\n- The documentation states that the reports are informational only and that\n  automated reclamation and cost calculations are not part of the capability.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-4 (P2): documentation explains the reports and safe reclamation steps.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":26906,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8864edd99ad3d1ec","agent_id":"adbd529e98eccbfe5","session_id":"05ddb1e2-6b5c-4b16-a274-ad31367aa2ce","uuid":"ad08108d-ae40-4af6-87fa-0cb360909f8a","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:37:42.154Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9016"}
