r the stale pipeline-run report: the configurable\n52\t  age threshold, retained artifacts, and the Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata\n53\t  source.\n54\t- A how-to section covering CSV export of either report.\n55\t- A how-to section on safe reclamation steps for idle workbenches and stale\n56\t  pipeline runs, making explicit that the reports are informational and\n57\t  reclamation/deletion is manual and out of the feature's scope.\n58\t- Cross-links from existing workbench and pipelines documentation to the new\n59\t  reporting topics where a reader would look for them.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- Given the shipped reports, when a reader opens the documentation, then the\n64\t  report descriptions (columns, data sources, configurable threshold, CSV\n65\t  export) match the implemented behavior in the web console.\n66\t- Given an administrator following the documented reclamation steps, when the\n67\t  steps are executed against a test project, then they are accurate and\n68\t  complete for both idle workbenches and stale pipeline runs.\n69\t- The documentation has been technically reviewed against the implemented\n70\t  reports by the team that built them, and review feedback is addressed.\n71\t- The documentation states that the reports are informational only and that\n72\t  automated reclamation and cost calculations are not part of the capability.\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- HLR-4 (P2): documentation explains the reports and safe reclamation steps.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8739fbd434aec2eb","agent_id":"a2b5ec70b38551f06","session_id":"05ddb1e2-6b5c-4b16-a274-ad31367aa2ce","uuid":"e19ef421-a631-4cca-9ec4-3c399df2f54a","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:39:16.396Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7cb25565757badd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
