{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-823cba081012b44d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9016-E001\n3\ttitle: Idle and stale resource reports in the web console\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 8\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Idle and stale resource reports in the web console\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers per-project idle and stale resource reporting in the RHOAI\n34\tweb console, giving cluster administrators visibility into reclaimable\n35\tcapacity. The console gains a report surface showing, per project, workbenches\n36\tthat have been idle (with their last activity, owner, and reserved resources)\n37\tand pipeline runs that are stale (completed runs older than a configurable age\n38\tthat still retain artifacts). Both reports can be exported as CSV.\n39\t\n40\tThe report data is sourced from existing platform telemetry: the notebook\n41\tcontroller's per-workbench activity tracking and Kubeflow Pipelines run\n42\tcompletion metadata. No changes are made to the notebook controller or to\n43\tKubeflow Pipelines — both keep working as-is and serve as read-only data\n44\tsources.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- A per-project idle-workbench report in the web console listing each\n49\t  workbench's last activity timestamp, owner, and reserved resources, sourced\n50\t  from the notebook controller's activity tracking.\n51\t- A per-project stale pipeline-run report listing completed runs older than a\n52\t  configurable age that retain artifacts, sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run\n53\t  metadata.\n54\t- A configurable age threshold for the stale pipeline-run report.\n55\t- CSV export of either report.\n56\t- Read-only reporting only: no automated or UI-initiated reclamation,\n57\t  deletion, or culling actions, and no cost/chargeback calculations (strategy\n58\t  out of scope).\n59\t- Screenshots or caption updates elsewhere in the console that fall out of\n60\t  this change are updated as part of the same change.\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- Given a project containing workbenches with differing activity, when an\n65\t  administrator opens the idle-workbench report, then each workbench is listed\n66\t  with its last activity timestamp, owner, and reserved resources, and the\n67\t  values match the notebook controller's activity tracking for that\n68\t  workbench.\n69\t- Given a project containing completed pipeline runs of differing ages, when\n70\t  an administrator opens the stale pipeline-run report with a given age\n71\t  threshold, then only completed runs older than the threshold that retain\n72\t  artifacts are listed, and the entries match Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n73\t- Given the stale pipeline-run report, when an administrator changes the\n74\t  configurable age threshold, then the report contents update accordingly.\n75\t- Given either report, when an administrator exports it as CSV, then the\n76\t  resulting file contains the report rows and columns as displayed.\n77\t- Given the reports, when reviewed, then no reclamation, deletion, or cost\n78\t  calculation actions are offered — the feature is informational only.\n79\t\n80\t## HLR Traceability\n81\t\n82\t- HLR-1 (P1): per-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner,\n83\t  reserved resources) sourced from the notebook controller's activity\n84\t  tracking.\n85\t- HLR-2 (P1): stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a\n86\t  configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines\n87\t  run metadata.\n88\t- HLR-3 (P2, bundled): CSV export of either report — shares the same report\n89\t  surfaces and data-fetch code as HLR-1/HLR-2, so it is delivered within this\n90\t  epic rather than as a separately schedulable deliverable.\n91\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a51edbcd628f5651","agent_id":"a474d40c0e52ae50f","session_id":"05ddb1e2-6b5c-4b16-a274-ad31367aa2ce","uuid":"f564faad-e9ef-4d70-a0b2-5f22cba479a3","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:42:35.981Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-823cba081012b44d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
